      {
        "id": 151433,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-26T19:57:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If \"Up to 5\" for Sacrosynct Matyr must be a positive integer, should cards that say \"select up to x targets\" also have a minumum of 1 target?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Making \"up to\" be a minimum of 1 would be a wide-ranging change.&nbsp; Here is a partial list of cards that might force unwanted effects, in rough order of how likely I think the edge cases are:</p>\n<p>Vicious Cyclone</p>\n<p>Inferno<br>The Predator's Eye<br>Disruptive Flechettes<br>Ball Lightning</p>\n<p>Gaussian Coil Blaster<br>Fueled Freeze<br>Construct Cataclysm<br>Temporal Grenade<br>RPG Launcher<br>Consecrated Ground<br>Crafty Assault<br>Localized Hurricane<br>Brainstorm<br>Innervation Ray<br>Hippocratic Oath<br>Robot Reclamation</p>\n<p>(For many of these, the edge case is \"Miss Information hasn't flipped, so there are no hostile targets on the board at all.\")</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:30:17.193Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
