      {
        "id": 151434,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-26T21:22:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If \"Up to 5\" for Sacrosynct Matyr must be a positive integer, should cards that say \"select up to x targets\" also have a minumum of 1 target?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;It says on the card&nbsp;  Sacrosanct Martyr&nbsp;  to deal herself radiant damage which is different wording than selecting X targets. &nbsp;If you choose zero than Fanatic isn't dealing herself any damage without any damage buffs. &nbsp;</p>",
